    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model. It returns `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, else `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 the owner's stored `possibleDuplicate` flag (set by `AssignPossibleDuplicate`) is true.\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 the email's domain shares a label with a known disposable-email domain (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) without being an exact blocked domain. Exact blocked domains are already rejected at create time by `ValidateOwnerEmailDomain`, so stored owners are flagged only for adjacent variants like `mailinator.net` or `sub.mailinator.com`.\n3. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 the owner's stored `capacityWarning` flag (set by `AssignCapacityWarning`, true at 40\u201349 of the 50 cap) is true.\n\nSince all three inputs derive from already-stored fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`, `email`), `riskFlag` is computed at read time rather than persisted \u2014 matching the project's existing pattern for derived owner fields (locality, timezone, telephoneDisplay, etc.).\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field).\n- **`OwnerRisk.java`** (new) \u2014 helper computing the flag and the disposable-adjacency check.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `riskFlag` via a MapStruct expression mapping, plus the import.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` (the `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` checkpoint asserting `$.riskFlag` is `false` for a fully-unique owner) passes, and the full `mvn test` run is `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
